WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.253
Eradication focuses on removing the cause of the incident,

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:05.355
not just quieting the visible symptom.

00:00:05.355 --> 00:00:07.808
If containment is about limiting harm now,

00:00:07.808 --> 00:00:11.662
eradication is about preventing the same issue from continuing or returning.

00:00:11.662 --> 00:00:16.567
The root cause might be a vulnerable system, an unsafe configuration, an exposed credential,

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:21.121
unauthorized access, a malicious artifact, a weak process, or a gap in ownership.

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:23.574
The right fix depends on the analysis.

00:00:23.574 --> 00:00:26.377
Sometimes eradication means patching and validating a system.

00:00:26.377 --> 00:00:29.530
Sometimes it means rebuilding a host, removing unauthorized access,

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.983
correcting cloud permissions, disabling an unsafe setting,

00:00:31.983 --> 00:00:35.486
or changing a process that allowed the problem to happen.

00:00:35.486 --> 00:00:40.041
This work should be authorized and tracked because eradication often touches production systems.

00:00:40.041 --> 00:00:40.741
Verification matters:

00:00:40.741 --> 00:00:44.946
the team should confirm that the cause was addressed and that the

00:00:44.946 --> 00:00:47.398
environment no longer shows the same behavior.

00:00:47.398 --> 00:00:49.150
Incomplete eradication creates recurrence risk.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:53.354
A clean-looking dashboard is not enough if the underlying path remains open.

00:00:53.354 --> 00:00:56.858
Good eradication produces evidence of the fix, the validation performed,

00:00:56.858 --> 00:00:59.661
and any residual risk that still needs ownership.

00:00:59.661 --> 00:01:04.215
Eradication also depends on knowing when a visible symptom is only a symptom.

00:01:04.215 --> 00:01:08.770
Resetting one account may not be enough if the access path remains open.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:12.974
Removing one artifact may not be enough if the vulnerable configuration remains.

00:01:12.974 --> 00:01:18.580
The response team should look for the condition that allowed the incident to happen or continue.
